# Data is large, externally sourced and reconstructible from the fetch scripts.
# What is version-controlled is the code that builds it and the manifest that
# records exactly which release was used -- not the bytes.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/ledger/
data/snapshots/
*.parquet
*.pt

# The stored results are committed. The manuscript says a reader can run the consistency checker
# rather than take its output on trust, and that all reported figures are regenerated by named
# scripts from the stored results. Neither is true without these 51 files: check_paper.py,
# check_consistency.py and build_figures.py read results/ and nothing else, and the raw data is not
# here to regenerate them from. 2.6 MB to make three claims in the paper checkable.
!results/.gitkeep

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
~$*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added before the first public push. The repository is public, so what is not here is a decision.

# Someone else's writing. The external reading of the manuscript was given to the authors and it is
# not theirs to publish. What it changed is recorded in REVISION-LOG.md instead.
penumbra-revizyon-notlari.md

# Run logs, not results. They carry the absolute path of the machine that produced them in 238
# places, and the numbers a reader needs are in the JSON beside them.
results/*.log

# Superseded manuscript drafts, 6.6 MB of binary between them. penumbra-revised.docx stays, because
# scripts/build_jmlr.py reads it and without it the .tex cannot be regenerated; these two are what
# it replaced.
paper/penumbra.docx
paper/penumbra-kbs.docx

# Build output that duplicates files already here. build_jmlr.py rewrites the figure copies and
# pack_jmlr.py rewrites the archive, so a fresh clone rebuilds both.
paper/jmlr/penumbra-overleaf.zip
paper/jmlr/figures/
paper/jmlr/_raw.tex

# The 600-dpi raster is a fallback for Word's SVG rendering. The manuscript uses the SVG, the LaTeX
# uses the PDF, and penumbra/figures.py writes all three, so this one is regenerated and not needed.
paper/Figures/*.png

# Empty run markers that nothing reads.
results/_*
